e negative if you show  things like uh disgust which is  generally wisely avoided that's minus  three points uh if you say anything  that's defensive it's minus two points  stonewalling especially that's that's  quite bad that's minus two points and  then anger uh  whining and sadness are all minus one  point but so what you can do then is you  can draw a graph where you look at  couples argument and instead of having  it as what was said you can translate it  into plus points and minus points and  you can look at how the conversation  evolves over time and that's essentially  what these equations do is they they  model how the conversation ebbs and  flows across the 15 minutes this  equation tells us about what someone's  going to say now you talked at the start  though about predicting divorce is that  a different equation or is that just  upping the ante from this equation uh  well so there's they kind of they link  in together so you can just look at how  overall how positive or negative people  are but the main point about this study  is that you're looking at the spirals of  positivity or negativity this term here  this influence term is really really  important looking at how well a  relationship is going  with one another and the the team have  come up with um a model a mathematical  model for how to present this this term  here you would have an identical  equation for the husband instantly but  if we just look at how much the husband  influences the wife so hw this here is  what the husband has just done at time t  and this here is the influence that he's  gonna have on his wife the shape of i is  the thing that's important rather than  the actual numbers themselves so if you  imagine  that um you're the the husband is quite  positive right so let's say he's more  positive than a particular threshold  t-plus right if he's like he's really  nice he's doing some really nice things  you know like buying i don't know  rings or like whatever like being really  