 and relaxed with  each other leave each other room to be  themselves couples with a really high  negativity threshold don't flip out over  small things i always thought that those  were the couples who uh who would end up  being the most successful but the team  found that it's actually the exact  opposite that's true that couples with a  really low negativity threshold  someone's where it's kind of like here  those were the ones who ended up having  the most success in the long term and  these are couples where  if something bothers them they speak up  about it and they mention it straight  away  and they don't let really small issues  end up becoming a really big deal but  they just addressed them and are  continually sort of resolving and  repairing the tiniest issues and dramas  in their relationship  number file is brought to you by the  mathematical sciences research institute  but we'd also like to thank audible.com  for their support of this video if you  spend time driving or commuting or  running or just relaxing what better way  to enrich your brain than with one of  the countless audio books stocked by  audible and if you sign up you can try  your first one for free  that first book could be by our very own  hannah fry the woman you just watched  reading her fantastic book the  mathematics of love have you ever  wondered why we're all so obsessed with  how hot a person is there it is it's on  audible waiting for you to download so  you can have hannah literally talking  mathematics right into your eardrums to  give audible a go and get that first  free book use the address  audible.com numberfile so they know you  came from here  and a huge thanks to audible for their  support of our videos

